WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.870
In 1965, GDP per person in
Zambia was 1,355 dollars.

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.950
In South Korea, 1,286.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.990
Zambia was slightly ahead.

4
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:18.190
By 2024: South Korea, 37,048 dollars.

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.410
Zambia, 1,343, slightly less than in 1965.

6
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.390
That puts Korea's 2024 figure
at about 28 times as high.

7
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.650
Was it luck?

8
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.230
Did Korea find more natural resources?

9
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.310
Why did their paths split so far apart?

10
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.810
In this mission, you'll test four big
theories of why some countries develop while

11
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.230
others stall.

12
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.030
Then you'll turn all four
lenses on these two countries,

13
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.230
and judge which explains the gap best.

14
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.790
Your mission: explain why Zambia's and
South Korea's paths split so far apart.
